# Performance Optimization (Refactor Mode)

Use these patterns when asked to optimize performance or when profiling indicates hot paths.

## Rendering Efficiency
- Use `React.memo` for expensive pure rows/items.
- Use `useMemo` for expensive derived values.
- Use `useCallback` only for stable function identity needs.
- Prefer stable keys from IDs, never array index for dynamic lists.

## Large Lists and Media
- Virtualize long lists where rendering volume is high.
- Defer offscreen media and use lazy image loading where appropriate.
- Keep image/video components lightweight on first paint.

## Code Splitting and Load Cost
- Split heavy route-level and modal-level code paths.
- Dynamically import heavy optional libraries.
- Keep the critical path free from nonessential dependencies.

## Data and Realtime Paths
- Avoid repeated refetch bursts from multiple effects.
- Batch or coalesce repeated requests where possible.
- Prevent N+1 style API usage from the client side.

## Optimization Guardrails
- Measure first (profiler, timings, bundle stats), then optimize.
- Do not add memoization everywhere by default.
- Do not trade readability for negligible gains.

## Performance Checklist
- [ ] Hot path identified and measured
- [ ] Optimization scoped to bottleneck
- [ ] No behavior regression
- [ ] Render count or latency improved
- [ ] Cleanup applied (no leftover experimental code)
